  "term": "porencephaly",
  "definition": "Porencephaly is a cortical brain malformation in which a cleft or cyst lined by white matter is present, often linked with ischemic or hemorrhagic injury. It can be associated with delayed growth and development, low muscle tone, seizures, one-sided spastic weakness, and abnormal head size or hydrocephalus.",
